; Wickmail DNS records template.
;
; Replace example.com, mail.example.com, 203.0.113.10, and the DKIM public key
; with host-specific values. These records are intentionally NOT in the flake;
; see ADR 0011 and docs/operations/deliverability.md.
;
; The DKIM selector and public key are produced by Rspamd (or another signer) on
; the mail host. The record below must match the key the outbound path signs
; with, so DMARC alignment holds.

$ORIGIN example.com.
$TTL 3600

; --- Mail host -------------------------------------------------------------
; The host that accepts inbound SMTP and submits outbound mail.
mail            IN A     203.0.113.10
; Publish AAAA only if the host has working IPv6 and an rDNS entry for it.
; mail          IN AAAA  2001:db8::10

; --- SPF -------------------------------------------------------------------
; Authorize only this host's MX to send for the domain. Soft-fail while
; ramping up, then hard-fail once deliverability is verified.
@               IN TXT   "v=spf1 mx -all"

; --- DKIM ------------------------------------------------------------------
; One TXT record per selector. `wickmail` is the suggested selector; it must
; match the Rspamd dkim_selector and the key used to sign outbound mail.
wickmail._domainkey IN TXT "v=DKIM1; k=rsa; p=<REPLACE_WITH_DKIM_PUBLIC_KEY>"

; --- DMARC -----------------------------------------------------------------
; Strict alignment for both SPF and DKIM. Start at p=none to collect reports,
; then move to quarantine and finally reject.
_dmarc          IN TXT   "v=DMARC1; p=quarantine; adkim=s; aspf=s; pct=100; rua=mailto:dmarc@example.com; ruf=mailto:dmarc@example.com; fo=1"

; --- TLS reporting (optional but recommended) ------------------------------
_smtp._tls      IN TXT   "v=TLSRPTv1; rua=mailto:tls@example.com"

; --- MTA-STS (optional) ----------------------------------------------------
; Enforce TLS for inbound mail by publishing a policy file at
; https://mta-sts.example.com/.well-known/mta-sts.txt and this record.
_mta-sts        IN TXT   "v=STSv1; id=REPLACE_WITH_POLICY_ID"
; mta-sts       IN CNAME  example.com.

; --- Reverse DNS (rDNS) ----------------------------------------------------
; PTR records are set at the hosting provider, not in this zone. The PTR for
; 203.0.113.10 must resolve to mail.example.com, and mail.example.com must
; forward-resolve to 203.0.113.10. See docs/operations/deliverability.md.
